WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.674
As Anne and Priscilla headed toward their new home in Halifax, Priscilla's happy chatter cheered up Anne, helping her forget her homesickness.

2
00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:15.866
"The boardinghouse is a big, old-fashioned, stone house on St. John Street," said Priscilla.

3
00:00:15.867 --> 00:00:21.755
"Your bedroom is at the front and overlooks old St. John's graveyard."

4
00:00:21.756 --> 00:00:29.641
"That sounds gruesome," said Anne, shivering. "I think I'd prefer a room at the back of the house."

5
00:00:29.642 --> 00:00:37.435
"No, you wouldn't," replied Priscilla. "The graveyard is a lovely place, and besides, it's not used anymore.

6
00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:41.542
There are enormous trees and a big stone wall."

7
00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:47.320
Before Anne went to sleep in her new room that night, she went to the window and looked out.

8
00:00:47.321 --> 00:00:50.301
The moon was shining over the graveyard.

9
00:00:50.302 --> 00:00:55.948
"I suppose the same moon is shining down on Green Gables," she mused.

10
00:00:55.949 --> 00:01:01.046
"But I won't think about it. I'm not even going to have a good cry.

11
00:01:01.047 --> 00:01:04.967
I'll be sensible and go straight to sleep!"

12
00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:10.466
The next day Anne and Priscilla went to Redmond College and enrolled as students.

13
00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:13.361
Gilbert and Charlie were nowhere to be seen.

14
00:01:13.362 --> 00:01:20.074
"I never thought I'd be glad to see a Sloane," said Priscilla as they crossed the campus on the way home.

15
00:01:20.075 --> 00:01:27.343
"But I'd welcome Charlie's goggle eyes almost ecstatically. At least they'd be familiar eyes."

16
00:01:27.344 --> 00:01:34.924
"I know." Anne sighed. "I feel as insignificant as a leaf in a forest here."

17
00:01:34.925 --> 00:01:42.684
"Anne, did you notice the girl who stood alone all morning—the pretty one with the brown suit and pink hat?" Priscilla asked.

18
00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:50.810
"Yes," said Anne. "I noticed her particularly because she seemed as lonely and friendless as I felt.

19
00:01:50.811 --> 00:01:54.422
I had you, of course, but she had no one."

20
00:01:54.423 --> 00:02:01.143
"She looked as though she wanted to approach us, but she did not," added Priscilla.

21
00:02:01.144 --> 00:02:06.813
After lunch Anne asked Priscilla if she wanted to take a stroll through St. John's graveyard.

22
00:02:06.814 --> 00:02:15.645
"I don't know that a graveyard is a very good place to go to cheer myself up, but it has such beautiful trees," said Anne.

23
00:02:15.646 --> 00:02:21.316
"I'll sit and shut my eyes and imagine I'm in the Avonlea woods."

24
00:02:21.317 --> 00:02:25.672
But as they strolled through the graveyard, Anne couldn't stop looking around.

25
00:02:25.673 --> 00:02:29.554
She was fascinated by the old gravestones.

26
00:02:29.555 --> 00:02:35.505
"'Here lies the body of Albert Crawford,'" Anne read from a worn, gray slab.

27
00:02:35.506 --> 00:02:42.591
"'He was a brave officer, the best of husbands, the best of fathers, the best of friends.

28
00:02:42.592 --> 00:02:48.855
He died October 29, 1792, aged 84 years.'

29
00:02:48.856 --> 00:02:52.852
He must have led an adventurous life, Priscilla!"

30
00:02:52.853 --> 00:02:57.107
"Look, Anne." Priscilla gestured toward the end of the path.

31
00:02:57.108 --> 00:03:02.857
"It's the girl we saw at Redmond College this morning! I've been watching her.

32
00:03:02.858 --> 00:03:07.736
She has started to walk toward us and then turned back at least five times!

33
00:03:07.737 --> 00:03:11.918
Maybe she's very shy. Let's go and meet her."

34
00:03:11.919 --> 00:03:16.876
They walked toward the stranger, who was sitting under an enormous willow tree.

35
00:03:16.877 --> 00:03:24.952
She was certainly very pretty, and still wore the fashionable brown suit and a pale pink hat with brown poppies.

36
00:03:24.953 --> 00:03:30.915
Priscilla and Anne suddenly felt very self-conscious in their unfashionable clothes from the country.

37
00:03:30.916 --> 00:03:34.832
For a moment both girls felt like turning back.

38
00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:36.851
But it was too late to retreat.

39
00:03:36.852 --> 00:03:41.901
The girl sprang up and came forward with an outstretched hand and a friendly smile.

40
00:03:41.902 --> 00:03:44.513
"Oh, I've been dying to meet you girls.

41
00:03:44.514 --> 00:03:48.803
I saw you at Redmond this morning," she said eagerly.

42
00:03:48.804 --> 00:03:54.712
"Wasn't it awful there? I was wishing I had stayed home and gotten married instead!"

43
00:03:54.713 --> 00:03:58.405
Anne and Priscilla both laughed at this surprising comment.

44
00:03:58.406 --> 00:04:05.171
The brown-eyed girl laughed too. "Come," she said. "Let's sit down and get acquainted.

45
00:04:05.172 --> 00:04:12.046
I know we're going to be friends—I knew when I saw you at Redmond, and I wanted to come and say hello."

46
00:04:12.047 --> 00:04:14.748
"Why didn't you?" asked Priscilla.

47
00:04:14.749 --> 00:04:19.697
"Because I simply couldn't make up my mind," the girl said sorrowfully.

48
00:04:19.698 --> 00:04:22.798
"I can never make up my mind about anything."

49
00:04:22.799 --> 00:04:26.373
"We thought you were too shy," said Anne.

50
00:04:26.374 --> 00:04:35.132
"No, no. I'm not shy. My name's Philippa Gordon— Phil for short. Call me Phil."

51
00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:38.782
"She's Priscilla Grant," said Anne, pointing.

52
00:04:38.783 --> 00:04:43.437
"And she's Anne Shirley," said Priscilla, pointing in turn.

53
00:04:43.438 --> 00:04:47.494
"And we're from the island," said both together.

54
00:04:47.495 --> 00:04:51.323
"I'm from Bolingbroke, Nova Scotia," said Philippa.

55
00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:56.772
"Bolingbroke!" exclaimed Anne. "That's where I was born."

56
00:04:56.773 --> 00:05:03.645
"Well, we're old neighbors, aren't we?" Phil laughed.

57
00:05:03.646 --> 00:05:11.803
"I don't know how you made up your mind to come to Redmond at all if you are really such an indecisive person," said Priscilla, amused.

58
00:05:11.804 --> 00:05:15.873
"Oh, I didn't! My father wanted me to go to college.

59
00:05:15.874 --> 00:05:21.144
I have heaps of brains," Phil chatted, "but it's such hard work to use them.

60
00:05:21.145 --> 00:05:24.945
My mother wanted me to get married, but I'm too young!

61
00:05:24.946 --> 00:05:30.006
Besides, how could I ever decide which man to marry?"

62
00:05:30.007 --> 00:05:32.876
"Were there so many?" Anne laughed.

63
00:05:32.877 --> 00:05:37.568
"Heaps. Boys like me a lot—they really do.

64
00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:42.730
But there were only two boys that mattered—Alec and Alonzo.

65
00:05:42.731 --> 00:05:45.735
The rest were all too young or too poor."

66
00:05:45.736 --> 00:05:49.127
"Do you love either of them?" asked Anne.

67
00:05:49.128 --> 00:05:54.510
"Oh no, I couldn't love anybody!" said Phil.

68
00:05:54.511 --> 00:05:57.963
"Being in love makes you a perfect slave, I think!

69
00:05:57.964 --> 00:06:03.982
I saw one handsome fellow this morning, though. His friend called him Gilbert."

70
00:06:03.983 --> 00:06:08.112
Anne felt a prick of annoyance and decided it was time to leave.

71
00:06:08.113 --> 00:06:12.599
"Don't go yet!" Phil said. "Let's meet tomorrow!"

72
00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:23.088
Anne and Priscilla could not resist Phil's cheerfulness and made plans to meet their first new friend again the next day.

